; claude: the browser's networking, from elm-playground's libs/networking
; (its tiny_libs.networking_* libraries), the part a browser needs:
; protocols/ (Url, Urlencoded, Http: RFC 3986, forms' queries, HTTP/1.1
; messages), tls/ (Asn1, Pem, X509, Tls13: a TLS 1.3 client, pure, bytes
; in and bytes out) and unix/ (Tcp, Worker, Tls_client, Http_client,
; Http_request: the sockets, the GET, and the same GET as a non-blocking
; machine stepped each frame). Its own copy, to grow (cookies,
; compression, keep-alive); the cryptography stays tiny_libs.crypto.
;
; Wrapped, as Network: the Playground links tiny_libs' networking (its
; Http and Multiplayer APIs, and the native platforms' Http.get), whose
; unwrapped modules have the same names -- two modules Url in one program
; would not link. Never written, though: the libraries using it say
; (flags (:standard -open Network)), and their code Url.parse,
; Http_request.start, ours rather than the Playground's.
(include_subdirs unqualified)

(library
 (name network)
 (wrapped true)
 (libraries
   unix
   threads.posix ; Worker's pool
   caps ; Cap.network, which every function opening a socket takes
   logs ; -v: the roots' file read
   tiny_libs.crypto ; the hashes, ciphers and signatures of TLS
   tiny_libs.core)) ; Base64 (PEM), Civil and Clock (certificates' dates)
